You can't actually use this method to determine how long a corpse is 
safe to eat. The check for taintedness only applies when you first begin 
to eat a corpse. If you stop for any reason and then begin eating the 
same corpse again, you can do so without worry about food poisoning. 
This does *not* apply if you've taken a bite of anything else in 
between, or if you've saved the game and restarted.
> 
> By the way, this trick sometimes fails, since once in a while the corpse
> will completely rot away and disappear while you're eating it, without
> you finishing it and then getting the good effects.
> 
The counter for the food rotting away has nothing to do with the 
taintedness check. You can use the above procedure to continue eating 
the corpse right up until it rots away. However, if you wait before 
*beginning* to eat the corpse, it will give you food poisoning long 
before that.

